Hi Bukola,
>From the IsoriX point of view, it seems you did things right!
Since you used the same isoscape and the "wild" calibration method, the difference in calibration function over the years must stem from differences in measurements in the calibration samples.
That could be biological or methodological.
If that is biological, the best would be to pool all the samples to capture as much of the real biological variation that is out there (and I would thus not discard anything).
I will let David Soto, the head of the isotope lab here at IZW, answer about which methodological aspects may be relevant to check.
Do give him a bit of time, since there is an isotope course here this week, so he is very busy.
Best,
Alex

