Hi Bukola and Alex,

Apologies for my slow response. From the methodological point of view, you should consider the hydrogen exchangeability properties of these organic materials. In order to ensure accurate and reproducible H isotope measurements among laboratories, analytical batches, etc, matrix‐equivalent organic reference materials are required for normalization according to the identical treatment principle.

Best regards,
David Soto

